  <h2>5. Antipodes: The Exact Opposite Point on Earth</h2>
  <p>
    An <strong>antipode</strong> is the spot diametrically opposite any location on the globe. You can easily calculate the antipode of any coordinate (φ, λ):
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Antipodal Latitude:</strong> Multiply your latitude by -1 (e.g., 40° N → 40° S).</li>
    <li><strong>Antipodal Longitude:</strong> If longitude is positive, subtract 180°; if negative, add 180° (e.g., -74° W → +106° E).</li>
  </ul>

